BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//Littoralicious//Terroir Piraeus//EN
X-WR-CALNAME:Piraeus — eat & drink checklist
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:piraeus-liste-1@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Garides saganaki — Whole shrimp baked in garlicky tomato with a splash of ouzo and feta melted through\, brought spitting in its two-handled pan.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ga-REE-dhes sa-ga-NA-kee. The one plate this harbour invented\, in the Mikrolimano fish houses of the early 1960s. Best: Dourabeis\, Mikrolimano — on its list as shrimp saganaki
LOCATION:Dourabeis\, Mikrolimano — on its list as shrimp saganaki
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Dourabeis+Akti+Dilaveri+29+Piraeus
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:piraeus-liste-2@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Psari sta karvouna — A whole fish chosen off the ice\, weighed in front of you\, grilled over charcoal and lifted off the bone at the table.
DESCRIPTION:Say: psa-REE sta kar-VOO-na. Ask the price per kilo before the scale moves: that sentence is the whole etiquette of the port. Best: Papaioannou\, Mikrolimano — the plain grill
LOCATION:Papaioannou\, Mikrolimano — the plain grill
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Papaioannou+Akti+Koumoundourou+42+Piraeus
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:piraeus-liste-3@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Marides & gavros tiganites — Whitebait and anchovy dusted in flour and fried whole\, heads and tails\, with lemon.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ma-REE-dhes\, GA-vros tee-ga-nee-TES. Always wild: the one fish on the ice a farm cannot fake\, and the cheapest. Best: Margaro\, Hatzikyriakio — no menu\, no bookings
LOCATION:Margaro\, Hatzikyriakio — no menu\, no bookings
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Margaro+Chatzikyriakou+126+Piraeus
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:piraeus-liste-4@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Kakavia — The fishermen's soup of small rockfish simmered with oil\, onion and potato until the flesh slides off the bone.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ka-ka-VYA. Named for the kakavi\, the tripod pot set on the sand\; the catch nobody would buy. Best: Varoulko Seaside\, Mikrolimano
LOCATION:Varoulko Seaside\, Mikrolimano
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Varoulko+Seaside+Akti+Koumoundourou+Piraeus
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:piraeus-liste-5@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Astakomakaronada — Spiny langouste cut into a light tomato sauce lifted with ouzo\, tossed through spaghetti until the pasta drinks the stock.
DESCRIPTION:Say: a-sta-ko-ma-ka-ro-NA-dha. The plate of money of the boom years on the crescent\, usually langouste rather than clawed lobster. Best: Papaioannou\, Mikrolimano
LOCATION:Papaioannou\, Mikrolimano
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Papaioannou+Akti+Koumoundourou+42+Piraeus
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:piraeus-liste-6@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Achinosalata — Sea-urchin roe scooped from the shell and dressed only with lemon and oil.
DESCRIPTION:Say: a-hee-no-sa-LA-ta. The rawest taste of the port\; eat it only where the urchins were opened that day. Best: Papaioannou\, Mikrolimano — the raw table
LOCATION:Papaioannou\, Mikrolimano — the raw table
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Papaioannou+Akti+Koumoundourou+42+Piraeus
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:piraeus-liste-7@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Taramosalata — Cured roe whipped with oil\, lemon and soaked bread into a pale\, airy dip.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ta-ra-mo-sa-LA-ta. Pale is right\; shocking pink means dye. Clean Monday is its day. Best: Dourabeis\, Mikrolimano — its own\, silky
LOCATION:Dourabeis\, Mikrolimano — its own\, silky
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Dourabeis+Akti+Dilaveri+29+Piraeus
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:piraeus-liste-8@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Mydia saganaki — Mussels in a spicy tomato and feta sauce\, the cousin of the shrimp dish the port invented.
DESCRIPTION:Say: MEE-dhya sa-ga-NA-kee. Cheap\, abundant\, and the backbone of the ouzeri table. Best: To Limanaki tou Giorgou\, Keratsini
LOCATION:To Limanaki tou Giorgou\, Keratsini
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=To+Limanaki+tou+Giorgou+Keratsini
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:piraeus-liste-9@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Bakaliaros skordalia — Salt cod fried in batter\, with a sharp garlic and potato or bread purée.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ba-ka-LYA-ros skor-dha-LYA. The ritual plate of 25 March\, Independence Day and the Annunciation. Best: To Koutouki tou Antoni\, Palaia Kokkinia
LOCATION:To Koutouki tou Antoni\, Palaia Kokkinia
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=To+Koutouki+tou+Antoni+Argyrokastrou+26+Piraeus
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:piraeus-liste-10@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Soutzoukakia smyrneika — Oval meat rolls with cumin and garlic\, simmered in tomato.
DESCRIPTION:Say: soo-dzoo-KA-kya smeer-NAY-ee-ka. Smyrna's dish\, which the refugees of 1922 carried into the new quarters behind the port. Best: Alargino\, Nikaia — handmade
LOCATION:Alargino\, Nikaia — handmade
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Alargino+Agiou+Ioannou+2+Nikaia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:piraeus-liste-11@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Kebab\, the Armenian way — Hand-ground mince with salt and pepper only\, grilled over charcoal and laid on pita.
DESCRIPTION:Say: keh-BAP. A survivor of Smyrna learned the grill in Kokkinia around 1972\; his children keep the one rule. Best: Souvlakia o Serkos\, Plateia Neraidas
LOCATION:Souvlakia o Serkos\, Plateia Neraidas
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Souvlakia+o+Serkos+Ionos+Dragoumi+39+Piraeus
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:piraeus-liste-12@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Pastourma — Air-cured beef under a rust-red crust of fenugreek\, garlic and paprika\, sliced paper-thin.
DESCRIPTION:Say: pa-stoor-MAS. The Cappadocian cure that came with 1922\, still made by hand. Best: Avakian\, Stoa Politou — four generations
LOCATION:Avakian\, Stoa Politou — four generations
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Avakian+Piraeus
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:piraeus-liste-13@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Piroski — A fried pocket of dough round cheese\, mince or potato\, eaten hot from the paper.
DESCRIPTION:Say: pee-RO-skee. The Pontic pie of Trebizond\, fried here from three in the morning since 1977. Best: Euxeinon\, Navarchou Notara — before midday
LOCATION:Euxeinon\, Navarchou Notara — before midday
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Euxeinon+Navarchou+Notara+50+Piraeus
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:piraeus-liste-14@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Galaktoboureko — Semolina custard baked in buttered phyllo and soaked in syrup while hot.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ga-lak-to-BOO-reh-ko. Since a milk round by donkey in 1909\, the slab the whole port measures against. Best: Mastronikolas\, Karaoli & Dimitriou 68
LOCATION:Mastronikolas\, Karaoli & Dimitriou 68
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mastronikolas+Karaoli+Dimitriou+68+Piraeus
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:piraeus-liste-15@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Bougatsa — Hand-pulled phyllo round custard or feta\, dusted with sugar and cinnamon.
DESCRIPTION:Say: boo-GA-tsa. Best in the small hours\, when the 24-hour workshops have just baked. Best: Bougatsa Pavlidi\, Petrou Ralli\, Nikaia
LOCATION:Bougatsa Pavlidi\, Petrou Ralli\, Nikaia
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bougatsa+Pavlidi+Petrou+Ralli+168+Nikaia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:piraeus-liste-16@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Retsina — Savatiano white with Aleppo-pine resin added in the ferment\, drunk cold with fried fish.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ret-SEE-na. The one wine the port can call its own\; a few rooms still draw it from the barrel. Best: To Eidikon\, Agios Dionysios — from the cellar under the floor
LOCATION:To Eidikon\, Agios Dionysios — from the cellar under the floor
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=To+Eidikon+Psaron+38+Piraeus
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:piraeus-liste-17@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Ouzo — Anise spirit that turns milk-white with water or ice\, ordered with meze to slow it down.
DESCRIPTION:Say: OO-zo. Reserved by EU law to Greece and Cyprus\; the port owns the ritual\, Lesvos the bottle. Best: To Yperokeaneion\, Hatzikyriakio
LOCATION:To Yperokeaneion\, Hatzikyriakio
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=To+Yperokeaneion+Marias+Chatzikyriakou+48+Piraeus
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:piraeus-liste-18@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Tsipouro — Pomace spirit\, usually without anise here\, ordered by the karafaki.
DESCRIPTION:Say: TSEE-poo-ro. The rougher cousin of ouzo\, distilled from what the wine press leaves behind. Best: Ikariotiko Kafeneio\, Aristeidou — with whatever plates arrive
LOCATION:Ikariotiko Kafeneio\, Aristeidou — with whatever plates arrive
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ikariotiko+Kafeneio+Aristeidou+17+Piraeus
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:piraeus-liste-19@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Ellinikos kafes — Fine coffee boiled slowly in a briki and served with its foam and grounds.
DESCRIPTION:Say: el-lee-nee-KOS ka-FES. Order it sketo\, metrio or glyko: the sugar goes in the pot\, never after. Best: O Stavros\, Stoa Kampanidi — among the market porters
LOCATION:O Stavros\, Stoa Kampanidi — among the market porters
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Stoa+Kampanidi+Piraeus
END:VTODO
END:VCALENDAR
